# === 1.3.0 additions ===

# Settings: WP-user auto-link
msgid "Auto-link logged-in WordPress users"
msgstr ""

msgid "Identify logged-in WordPress users via their account email"
msgstr ""

msgid "Existing tokens are reused. If a logged-in user has no token yet, a new one is created automatically (source: wp_user_auto). Turn this off if you do not want tokens for non-form visitors (admins, customers, forum members)."
msgstr ""

# Settings: FluentCRM data source
msgid "FluentCRM data source"
msgstr ""

msgid "When FluentCRM is active, contact fields and custom_values from FluentCRM can be merged into PSFID resolver fields. Forms then pre-fill with the latest CRM data automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "Merge FluentCRM data"
msgstr ""

msgid "Read contact fields and custom_values from FluentCRM into PSFID"
msgstr ""

msgid "FluentCRM wins on conflicts: if both PSFID and FluentCRM have a value for the same field, the FluentCRM value is used. Empty FluentCRM values never overwrite PSFID data."
msgstr ""

msgid "Developers: restrict which fields are merged via the %s filter."
msgstr ""

# Help: cookies sectie
msgid "Logged-in WordPress user: matched on account email. Existing token reused, otherwise a new one is created (source: wp_user_auto)."
msgstr ""

# Help: WP-user sectie
msgid "Automatic WordPress user recognition"
msgstr ""

msgid "New in 1.3.0"
msgstr ""

msgid "Logged-in WordPress users are automatically linked to a Pure Smart Form ID token via their account email address. This means forms pre-fill with the user's known data without them needing to click a link with a token."
msgstr ""

msgid "When to use it"
msgstr ""

msgid "Member portals where users fill in forms regularly (coaching, training, support)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Customer accounts in WooCommerce where checkout-related forms should pre-fill"
msgstr ""

msgid "Internal staff forms where the WordPress login is enough identification"
msgstr ""

msgid "When to turn it off"
msgstr ""

msgid "On sites with many logged-in non-form visitors (forum members, free-trial accounts, large customer base) you may not want a token generated for every visitor who never fills in a form. Turn the setting off in %s."
msgstr ""

msgid "Settings -> Identification fallbacks"
msgstr ""

msgid "Auto-generated tokens have source \"wp_user_auto\" in the Tokens overview, so you can identify and clean them up separately if needed."
msgstr ""

# Help: FC-source sectie
msgid "FluentCRM as data source"
msgstr ""

msgid "When FluentCRM is active, Pure Smart Form ID can read contact data directly from FluentCRM and use it for form pre-fill and shortcodes. This makes FluentCRM the master record for contact information; PSFID tokens stay leading for identification."
msgstr ""

msgid "What gets merged"
msgstr ""

msgid "Standard fields: first_name, last_name, email, phone, company, address_line_1, address_line_2, postal_code, city, state, country"
msgstr ""

msgid "All custom_values stored on the FluentCRM contact"
msgstr ""

msgid "Conflict rule"
msgstr ""

msgid "FluentCRM wins when both PSFID and FluentCRM have a value for the same key. Empty FluentCRM values never overwrite PSFID data, so a blank custom field will not erase a value the visitor previously entered through a form."
msgstr ""

msgid "Restricting which fields are merged"
msgstr ""

msgid "By default, all available fields are merged. To limit this, add a filter in your theme or a custom plugin:"
msgstr ""

